# Build / dependency / secret artifacts
node_modules/
dist/
out/
.env
.env.local
*.log
.DS_Store

# Credential / key file extensions — defense in depth. The realistic paths
# (out/, .env) are already covered above; these catch a contributor's other
# tooling habits (openssl, java keystores, ad-hoc *-key.json files) before
# they reach a commit.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.crt
*.cer
*-key.json
*-keys.json
*.private.json
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519

# Other env conventions (direnv, per-environment files). .env.example is the
# one tracked exception — it carries placeholders only.
.envrc
*.env
*.env.*
!.env.example

# Archived OB 3.0 prototype: build, deps, throwaway signing keys, context cache
archive/node_modules/
archive/dist/
archive/out/
archive/.env
archive/.env.local

# Archived OB 3.0 prototype: internal strategy/demo material — canonical home stays in
# the private orchestration vault, not this public repo. Kept locally for
# reference but never committed here.
archive/end-user-ux-research.md
archive/DEMO.md
archive/screencast-script.md

# Migration guard (retire-spike, 2026-08). `git mv` moves tracked files only,
# so pulling the rename into an existing clone deletes the tracked spike/ files
# and strands every untracked one — now un-ignored, and one `git add -A` from a
# permanent public history.
#
# Deliberately the whole directory rather than the specific leftovers. Naming
# them individually missed a case: the nested .gitignore at
# verifier-spike/verifiers/spruce/.gitignore travelled to archive/ with the
# code, so the `/target` rule that had been ignoring 1.4GB of Rust build output
# stopped applying at the old path. Ignore rules live inside a moved tree too,
# and they leave with it.
#
# Nothing should exist at spike/ anymore, so this hides nothing worth seeing.
# Remove it once no working copy has a spike/ leftover.
spike/

# python build artifacts
generator/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Font-subsetting venv (generator/embed_fonts.py needs fonttools + brotli; its
# docstring prescribes exactly this). Build-time only — the OUTPUT (fonts.css,
# page_fonts.css and their integrity manifests) is committed, the toolchain is not.
.fontvenv/

# OG card composition intermediates (imaging/og.py -> temp SVGs); only the
# rasterized badges/*.og.png is committed.
imaging/.og-build/
.worktrees
